            <ArticleTitle>Reversible posterior leukoencephalopathy syndrome following sunitinib therapy: a case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>139e-142e</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1700/1190.13216</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sunitinib is one of the standard targeted therapies used in metastatic renal cell carcinoma. It is generally a reasonably tolerated oral systemic therapy but can be occasionally associated with life-threatening toxicities. We present a case of reversible posterior encephalopathy, which is a rare but recognised side effect of the treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
